# A row's context menu (decision 086): one at a time, on the island's shown
# card, over its rows; it goes with its card, its row, a dialog, typing.

scenario: opened by the keys, its first item is lit
panel search menu
tile search                         -> Expanded expanded=search draft=empty
menu search 1                       -> menu=search/1 lit=0
menu-close                          -> menu=none Expanded draft=empty   # the card and its field stay

scenario: opened by a right-click, nothing is lit until the pointer moves onto an item
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 2 pointer               -> menu=search/2 lit=none
menu-light 2                        -> lit=2
menu-light none                     -> lit=none
menu-light 1                        -> lit=none                         # a dim item can't be lit
menu-light 7                        -> lit=none                         # nor one past the end

scenario: the keys pass over dim items and go round
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1                       -> lit=0
menu-step 1                         -> lit=2                            # Run is dim: skipped
menu-step 1                         -> lit=0                            # round to the first
menu-step -1                        -> lit=2                            # and back round to the last
menu-end first                      -> lit=0
menu-end last                       -> lit=2
menu-letter r                       -> lit=2                            # Reveal: Run is dim
menu-letter o                       -> lit=0

scenario: only on a row that has a menu, on the card that's shown
panel search menu
panel other
menu search 1                       -> menu=none                        # not shown
tile search
menu search 0                       -> menu=none                        # the field's row has none
menu other 1                        -> menu=none                        # not this card
menu search 9                       -> menu=none                        # no such row

scenario: one at a time: another row's replaces it
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1
menu search 2                       -> menu=search/2 lit=0

scenario: it goes with its card
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1
esc                                 -> menu=none Idle

scenario: typing closes it: the rows under it change
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1
type a                              -> menu=none draft=a

scenario: scrolling the list closes it, a dialog covers it
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1
wheel search results 0 40 200       -> menu=none
menu search 1
ask search                          -> menu=none dialog=search
menu search 1                       -> menu=none                        # not under a dialog

scenario: a republish that keeps its items leaves it open; new items close it
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1
panel search menu                   -> menu=search/1 lit=0              # an icon arrived: the same items
panel search menu=changed           -> menu=none

scenario: an open menu holds the card open, like typing
panel search menu
tile search
menu search 1
wait 60000                          -> Expanded menu=search/1
menu-close
wait 60000                          -> Idle
